# Copied to .gitattributes in the published repository by scripts/publish.sh.
#
# Named without the leading dot on purpose, for the same reason publish/gitignore is: a real .gitattributes in publish/ would apply to this directory of the source repository rather than to the published one.
#
# This is the file that matters more of the two. The published repository is the one students clone, and Git for Windows sets core.autocrlf=true in its installer --- so without this, a student on Windows edits one line of a notebook and gets a diff claiming the whole file changed.
# The course asks them to read diffs; the first one they read should not be a lie.

# Normalise to LF in the repository whatever the committing machine uses.
* text=auto eol=lf

# A CR at the end of a shebang makes the kernel look for an interpreter whose name ends in a carriage return, and the error then names a file that visibly exists.
*.sh    text eol=lf

# The types the published repository is actually made of. It holds the built site plus the environment a Codespace needs, so this list is shorter than the source repository's --- no .lua, .scss or .qmd ever arrives here.
*.md    text eol=lf
*.tex   text eol=lf
*.html  text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf
*.svg   text eol=lf
*.ipynb text eol=lf

# Binary.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
# The decks' movies, in slides/media/ and copied into the built site beside the decks that play them.
*.mp4   binary

# The built site. Two things follow from marking it generated, and both are wanted:
# GitHub stops counting it towards the repository's language bar, which would otherwise read "HTML 99%" --- a fact about Quarto's output rather than about this course --- and it collapses docs/ out of pull request diffs by default.
#
# Only this repository has a docs/, which is the whole reason the two .gitattributes files are separate rather than one file copied twice.
docs/** linguist-generated
